                <pb facs="0653" n="611" sameAs="frus:frus1863p1/pg611"/>

                <head ana="#head_untitled-missing-head-in-printed-volume">[Untitled]</head>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Southern District of Florida:</hi></p>
                <p>Now comes Stephen Roberts, and, being duly sworn, deposes and says that he is by
                    occupation a Bahama pilot; that on the fifth day of November, A. D. 1862, he was
                    engaged as pilot on board the United States commissioned ship of-war the
                    Octorara; that on said day the said ship-of-war Octorara captured a schooner
                    called the Elias Reed; that the capture was made on the Bahama banks, about
                    midway between Little Abaco island on the south and the range of keys on the
                    north. Deponent believes the channel in which the Elias Reed was captured to be
                    at least nine and a half miles wide at the place of capture. The captured vessel
                    was just about in mid-channel, and cannot have been less than four miles from
                    the nearest point of land at the time of seizure.</p>
                <p rendition="#right">STEPHEN X ROBERTS.</p>
                <p>Subscribed and sworn before me this 29th day of November, 1862.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>GEORGE D. ALLEN, <hi rendition="#italic">Clerk United States District
                            Court.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
